const e="kerala-school-sasthrolsavam-it-fair",h=2025,t="Read, as page images because the PDF text is in a legacy font, the Malayalam manual's order and foreword, chapters 1 to 5 (general rules, conduct at the four levels, committees, appeals, championship), chapter 10 (IT Fair, pp.165-179) and the entry forms of Annexure I. Chapters 6 to 9 (the other fairs) and Annexure II (Skill Festival) were not read for rules: only their item lists are named under 'other'. The manual prints no dates, no venue, no contacts and no cash award amounts, so the dates and venue are 'To be announced'. The manual says nothing about a registration fee at school level; the Rs 20 is for sub-district classes 9 to 12. The IT Fair entry forms in the manual are only for the sub-district level. For UP Malayalam Typing the manual says only Part 1 is held and does not print how its score is scaled to 100. The IT Quiz question syllabus is not printed (KITE sets it each year). Chapter 3 committee duties that only concern the organisers (accounts, lights, pandal, publicity) are not copied. The ICT Teaching Aid item (codes 434-436) is a teachers' competition and is listed under 'other'. The word 'techniques' is used for the Malayalam word sanketham in the Multimedia Presentation criteria.",a=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam, IT Fair (UP, HS and HSS/VHSS). Read these rules before you register a student.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"All IT Fair items are done on the spot, on computers the organisers give you. No outside products and no personal digital gadgets (storage devices, mobile phones) are allowed. Entries are made online by the Headmaster or Principal.","Notes":["A student may take part in only one item of the IT Fair (or of any one fair), and may also take part in the quiz of any one fair.","Items scoring below 60% are not graded. Grades: A 80% and above, B 70% to 79%, C 60% to 69%."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Kerala School Sasthrolsavam is the name of the Science, Mathematics, Social Science, Work Experience (Pravrutti Parichaya) and IT fairs for children in LP, UP, HS, HSS and VHSS classes of Government, Aided and Unaided (recognised) schools of the General Education Department. This page is for the IT Fair.","This manual makes all earlier science, maths, social science, work experience and IT fair manuals and rules void.","The competitions from school level to state level are held on the dates in the education calendar of the General Education Department, or as the Director of General Education directs. Dates: {{EventDates}}","The aims include growing scientific and IT interest and research interest in students, giving them practice in using what they learn in daily life, introducing free software and new technology, letting them make creative products with digital media, and learning the computer language.","All Sasthrolsavam competitions (club level competitions) from sub-district to state level are held online. Entry is done online by the Headmaster or Principal.","The fair must follow the Green Protocol fully.","Only items that can keep children safe may be held at any level. Organisers take special care to put all safety measures in place.","Video recording of all item competitions from sub-district to state level is a must. For on-the-spot competitions, video is recorded when the products are complete. The Programme Committee is responsible for this.","Each fair is organised by the science, maths, social science, work experience and IT clubs (or the club association or council) of that level: the school club at school level, and the sub-district, revenue district and state association or council above that.","The IT Fair items are the same at every level, and are held separately for UP, HS and HSS/VHSS.","A competitor who also has exhibits must take part in the exhibition of their products at school, sub-district, revenue district and state levels.","A competitor at the state fair prepares a short description of their exhibit, with photographs if wanted, and gives it at competition time."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Students of Government, Aided and Unaided (recognised) schools under the General Education Department may take part.","There are four categories: Category I is classes 1 to 4, Category II is classes 5 to 7, Category III is classes 8 to 10 and Category IV is classes 11 and 12. The IT Fair has no Category I (no LP level).","Competitions in Categories I and II end at sub-district level. Competitions in Categories III and IV go up to state level.","A student may take part in only one item in any one of the Science, Maths, Social Science, Work Experience and IT fairs. The student may also take part in the quiz of any one fair.","Students who win first place with A grade at school level may take part at sub-district level.","In HS and HSS/VHSS, only students who win first or second place with A grade at sub-district level may take part at revenue district level. Only students who win first or second place with A grade at revenue district level may go on to the upper level.","At most two participants for one item from a sub-district or a revenue district may take part in the upper-level competition. This follows the judgement of the Hon'ble High Court of Kerala (W.A. No. 1178/2017, 22.6.2017).","Schools at the sub-district fair must be affiliated to the sub-district science, maths, social science, work experience and IT club association or council. Sub-districts at the revenue district fair, and revenue districts at the state fair, must be affiliated to the club association or council of that level.","To take part at sub-district level, bring the school-level certificate attested by the Headmaster.","To take part at revenue district level, bring a recognition certificate from the school Headmaster, attested by the Sub-district Education Officer.","To take part at state level, bring a recognition certificate from the school Headmaster, attested by the Deputy Director of Education.","Upload the student's photograph when you register. Each competitor also carries an identity card (a school-issued card with the child's photograph, school seal and the Principal's or Headmaster's signature).","HSS and VHSS are treated as one unit at sub-district level."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Students' online entries are made by the Headmaster or Principal. They must be done with great care.","Uploading each student's photograph is a must at registration.","The full responsibility for the online entries lies with the Headmaster or Principal.","The sub-district IT Fair entry form shows: school code, school name, phone, email, section (UP, HS or HSS/VHSS), the name and phone of the escorting teacher, and for each item the name, class, admission number and gender of each competitor.","The Principal or Headmaster signs the entry form with the school seal.","After the sub-district fair, register online the list of competitors chosen for the revenue district fair.","Each school needs an escorting teacher. If girls take part, women teachers must go as escorting teachers.","Every school team brings its own escorting teachers. For a revenue district team, the sub-district education officers and the sub-district secretary are the joint team managers.","Competition code numbers are given by the Director of General Education's office. The committee gives each district its code numbers and stall numbers."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees","Items":["Registration fee at sub-district level: {{SubDistrictRegistrationFee}}.","Appeal fees: school level {{AppealFeeSchool}}; sub-district {{AppealFeeSubDistrict}}; revenue district {{AppealFeeRevenueDistrict}}; state {{AppealFeeState}}; higher appeal {{AppealFeeHigher}}.","If an appeal is decided in your favour, the fee is returned. If not, the fee goes to the organising committee fund.","A new certificate: {{CertificateReissueFee}}, sent with the application, if the issued certificate is lost or has errors."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates","Items":["Dates: {{EventDates}}","The IT Quiz date and time are decided and announced by KITE every year.","The theme for the Multimedia Presentation (Composition and Presentation) is published one month before the competition. The subject within the theme is given 10 minutes before the competition starts.","The topic for Digital Painting, Animation, Web Page Designing and Scratch Project is given 10 minutes before the competition starts."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["Venue: {{Venue}}","Revenue district and sub-district fairs are held in a school chosen by the education officers and the club secretaries. Every level has a Programme Committee."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Levels and Qualification","Items":["The levels are school, sub-district, revenue district and state.","School level: held in one day. Every student of the school gets a chance, by category. The school IT club organises it and the Headmaster or Principal leads it (through the SITC for the quiz). Only students with first place and A grade in an item go to sub-district. If nobody gets first place with A grade, nobody is sent for that item.","If two students share first place or second place with equal marks, the one who goes up is chosen by adding the total marks and the marks for the first evaluation criterion.","If a single student is the only competitor in an item, the student goes to sub-district only if the student's performance earns a grade.","Sub-district: a two-day fair, held separately for UP, HS and HSS/VHSS.","Revenue district: a two-day fair for HS and HSS/VHSS. Only the first and second place winners of the sub-district fair take part.","State: a three-day fair. All revenue districts take part.","Winners at school level get certificates. Winners at sub-district and revenue district levels get certificates and incentive prizes.","The first three places in each item at state level get a certificate, a cash award and honours.","UP (Category II) competitions end at sub-district level."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Team Managers and Escorting Teachers","Items":["At the revenue district fair, the manager of each sub-district team is the sub-district education officer, and the sub-district secretaries are joint team managers.","At the state fair, each revenue district team has a team manager and escorting teachers for every section. The district association secretaries are joint team managers.","Women teachers must go with girls as escorting teachers.","Each school sending children to a sub-district fair appoints teachers to look after the children. Women teachers look after the girls. These teachers take full responsibility for the children."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct","Items":["All IT Fair competitions are held on the spot.","Nothing made outside the venue is allowed. Personal digital gadgets (storage devices, mobile phones and similar) are not allowed.","The organising committee gives the computers. Each competitor gets a computer by lot before the competition.","A competitor who is not at the right place at the right time is disqualified. The schedule is followed strictly. Rules and conditions of each item are announced on the stage before the competition begins.","Students, teachers and others who try to spoil the fair by acting without respect, without discipline or by provoking, face proper punishment, including disqualification, and departmental action as well.","After the competition, all products are saved on CD and kept for one year by the Programme Committee.","Competitors get a meal at the venue. On the judging day the food is given at the stalls. A competitor who goes away without taking part in the exhibition must tell the Programme Committee in writing."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging","Items":["Judges must be fair, experienced and able people. A biodata and a declaration of truth (Annexure) are taken from each judge. At every level there must be three people for judging.","A person may not be appointed a judge for more than two years in the fair and related competitions. A sub-district judge cannot judge at the revenue district fair of the same district. A district-level judge cannot judge the state fair that year.","A judge must make a declaration that no relative or student of the judge takes part in the competition the judge judges, and that the judge will judge fairly.","A score sheet has no cutting or correction. If a correction cannot be avoided, the judge who gave the marks signs it in full. Each judge gives each child's evaluation sheet (with remarks) with the score sheet.","Mark lists and tabulation sheets are printed and kept for one year, at the sub-district education office or the Deputy Director of Education's office, to be shown to the appeal committee or higher officers.","Items that score below 60% are not graded. Items scoring 60% or more are in three grades: A (80% and above) 5 points, B (70% to 79%) 3 points, C (60% to 69%) 1 point.","For the IT Quiz, the grade uses the percentile: (score of the participant / highest score in the competition) x 100%.","For each item, the marks are out of 100 and the place and the grade come from the total."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Points and Championship","Items":["Grade points: A 5, B 3, C 1.","Place points: first place 5 points, second place 3 points, third place 1 point.","A championship is worked out from the total of grade points and place points. If there is a tie, the number of first places is counted.","Sub-district: the best school in each of LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS is found from the total points of all the fairs. The best-performing schools in each fair are also found.","Revenue district: the best sub-districts and schools are found. The HS and HSS/VHSS championships are decided by the total points of the five fairs.","State: the best districts, sub-districts and schools are found, in the same way as for revenue districts.","The ICT Teaching Aid, talent search, magazine, seminars and similar competitions do not count for the championship."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Certificates and Trophies","Items":["Competitors who win grades get certificates from school level up.","Winners at sub-district and revenue district levels get certificates and incentive prizes.","At state level the first three places in each item get a certificate, a cash award and honours.","Certificates and trophies are given out on the days of the competitions. Trophies not given out are counted and handed to the Deputy Director of Education. The team manager or escorting teacher signs the trophy register to show the trophies were received.","Championships, their certificates and special honours are given at the closing ceremony.","An everrolling trophy or shield is valid for ten years. After that, if the donor does not give a new one, the Director of General Education withdraws it."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Appeals","Items":["An appeal committee is formed at every level to decide complaints about results. Its decision is final and follows the High Court order and this manual.","Make the complaint within {{AppealTimeLimit}}. A later appeal is not accepted for any reason.","At sub-district and revenue district levels, the complaint is made on the set form through the escorting teacher (sub-district) or the team manager (revenue district), with the appeal fee. At state level it is made through the revenue district team manager or joint team manager. Only complaints sent this way are considered.","The appeal form asks for: the student's name, school, revenue district, the item, code number, the place obtained, the date and time of the event, the date results were announced, the reason for the appeal, the signature of the competitor and the team manager.","School level: the appeal committee has the Principal or Headmaster and the school science, maths, social science, work experience and IT club coordinators. It checks that only the winner with A grade and first place goes to sub-district.","Sub-district: the appeal committee has the District Education Officer (chair), the Sub-district Education Officer (vice chair), RDD, AD, the General Convener and an expert in the subject.","Revenue district: the Deputy Director of Education (chair), RDD or AD (vice chair), the District Education Officer, the KITE District Coordinator and an expert or regional foreman.","State: the Director of General Education (chair), the Additional Director (Academic) (vice chair), the Directors of Higher Secondary and Vocational Higher Secondary, the KITE vice-chairman and executive director, and experts.","Before an order is issued on an appeal to a higher fair, the committee must make sure that only two competitors from a sub-district or revenue district go up for each item. If a third competitor is allowed by a court or appeal officers, the results of all qualified competitors are checked again so that only two go up.","The appeal committee gives its decision in a written order, on the set order form."]},{"Key":"reporting","Title":"Results","Items":["Results are made and uploaded online. Points are shown on the score board as the competitions go on.","Score sheets, remark sheets, tabulation sheets and the stage manager's report are collected after each competition.","Winners' lists are made (with the Kite) and given to the upper levels."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Fairs and Items (not in this template)","Items":["Science Fair (chapter 6): items by section (LP: Collections, Charts, Simple Experiments, Environmental Observation Presentation, Science Quiz; UP, HS and HSS/VHSS: Working Model, Still Model, Research Type Project, Improvised Experiment, Investigatory Project, Quiz, Science Drama, seminars and more).","Mathematics Fair (chapter 7): Number Chart, Geometrical Chart, Other Chart, Still Model, Working Model, Pure Construction, Geogebra Construction, Puzzle, Game, Single Project, Group Project, Quiz, Teaching Aid and Magazine, with the Bhaskaracharya Seminar and the Srinivasa Ramanujan Paper Presentation.","Social Science Fair (chapter 8): Atlas Making, Working Model, Still Model, Local History Writing, Elocution, Charithra Seminar, Quiz, Teaching Aid, Talent Search and News Reading.","Work Experience Fair, Pravrutti Parichaya (chapter 9): exhibition and on-the-spot items such as Bamboo products, Book binding, Clay modelling, Embroidery, Paper craft and Wood work.","ICT Teaching Aid (UP, HS and HSS teachers only, item codes 434, 435 and 436): teachers show self-made ICT teaching resources, with the Headmaster's certificate and a demo of up to 15 minutes. It is a teachers' competition and is not in this template.","Kerala School Skill Festival (Annexure II): a separate festival for Vocational Higher Secondary students (Innovision, SkillCraft, SkillServe and on-the-spot skill items)."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 (PDF, Malayalam)","Url":"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/entry_forms/sasthrolsavam_manual_2025.pdf"},{"Title":"Sasthrolsavam 2026 item list","Url":"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/index.php/Home/item_list"}]}`),i=[],o=[{AgeGroup:"IT UP",Source:"Manual 2025 pp.3, 165 (UP section)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["UP is classes 5 to 7 (Category II). The IT Fair for UP has three items: Digital Painting, Malayalam Typing and IT Quiz.","UP competitions end at sub-district level.","The UP competitions are held separately from HS and HSS/VHSS at school, and sub-district levels."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- UP is classes 5 to 7 (Category II). The IT Fair for UP has three items: Digital Painting, Malayalam Typing and IT Quiz.
- UP competitions end at sub-district level.
- The UP competitions are held separately from HS and HSS/VHSS at school, and sub-district levels.`},{AgeGroup:"IT HS",Source:"Manual 2025 pp.3, 165 (HS section)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["HS is classes 8 to 10 (Category III). The IT Fair for HS has seven items: IT Quiz, Digital Painting, Malayalam Typing and Designing, Scratch Programming, Composition and Presentation, Web Page Designing and Animation.","HS competitions go up to state level."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- HS is classes 8 to 10 (Category III). The IT Fair for HS has seven items: IT Quiz, Digital Painting, Malayalam Typing and Designing, Scratch Programming, Composition and Presentation, Web Page Designing and Animation.
- HS competitions go up to state level.`},{AgeGroup:"IT HSS/VHSS",Source:"Manual 2025 pp.3, 10, 165 (HSS/VHSS section)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["HSS/VHSS is classes 11 and 12 (Category IV). The IT Fair has seven items, the same as HS.","HSS and VHSS are treated as one unit.","HSS/VHSS competitions go up to state level."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- HSS/VHSS is classes 11 and 12 (Category IV). The IT Fair has seven items, the same as HS.
- HSS and VHSS are treated as one unit.
- HSS/VHSS competitions go up to state level.`}],n=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"IT Quiz","Source":"Manual 2025 ch.10 IT Fair p.166-167 (a. IT Quiz)","Sections":{"About":["IT changes every day. The IT Quiz tests the students' ability in this field."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Quizzes at sub-district, revenue district and state levels use a common question paper that KITE prepares at state level.","KITE decides and announces the time and date every year.","School level: the Principal or Headmaster leads, through the SITC, with separate quizzes for UP, HS and HSS/VHSS. The school SRG prepares the questions.","Sub-district: led by the Sub-district Education Officer, with separate quizzes for UP, HS and HSS/VHSS.","Revenue district: led by the Deputy Director of Education. In HS and HSS/VHSS, the first and second place winners at sub-district take part.","State: in HS and HSS/VHSS, the first and second place winners of the revenue district quiz may take part. The first three at state level get a certificate and a cash award."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The grade uses the percentile: (score of the participant / highest score in the competition) x 100%."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- IT changes every day. The IT Quiz tests the students' ability in this field.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Quizzes at sub-district, revenue district and state levels use a common question paper that KITE prepares at state level.\\n- KITE decides and announces the time and date every year.\\n- School level: the Principal or Headmaster leads, through the SITC, with separate quizzes for UP, HS and HSS/VHSS. The school SRG prepares the questions.\\n- Sub-district: led by the Sub-district Education Officer, with separate quizzes for UP, HS and HSS/VHSS.\\n- Revenue district: led by the Deputy Director of Education. In HS and HSS/VHSS, the first and second place winners at sub-district take part.\\n- State: in HS and HSS/VHSS, the first and second place winners of the revenue district quiz may take part. The first three at state level get a certificate and a cash award.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The grade uses the percentile: (score of the participant / highest score in the competition) x 100%."},{"Title":"Digital Painting","Source":"Manual 2025 ch.10 IT Fair pp.171-172 (d. Digital Painting)","Sections":{"About":["The aim is to grow the student's creative and artistic skill with digital technology. The picture follows the general grammar of painting, is true to the topic, and uses colours, lines and composition in a new way."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 1 hour."],"Rules":["The topic is given 10 minutes before the competition begins.","The picture is made on a canvas of the size given.","Use one of Kolour Paint, Krita or GIMP, available on the KITE Ubuntu OS."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Fit of the picture to the topic, and freshness of the idea: 25%.","Proportion of the forms in the picture: 25%.","Use of colours, tonal variation, harmony and contrast: 25%.","Skilled use of digital technology and how pleasing the picture is: 25%."],"Points":["Total 100%: 25 for each of the four criteria."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The aim is to grow the student's creative and artistic skill with digital technology. The picture follows the general grammar of painting, is true to the topic, and uses colours, lines and composition in a new way.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time: 1 hour.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The topic is given 10 minutes before the competition begins.\\n- The picture is made on a canvas of the size given.\\n- Use one of Kolour Paint, Krita or GIMP, available on the KITE Ubuntu OS.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Fit of the picture to the topic, and freshness of the idea: 25%.\\n- Proportion of the forms in the picture: 25%.\\n- Use of colours, tonal variation, harmony and contrast: 25%.\\n- Skilled use of digital technology and how pleasing the picture is: 25%.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100%: 25 for each of the four criteria."},{"Title":"Malayalam Typing","Source":"Manual 2025 ch.10 IT Fair pp.167-169 (b. Malayalam Documentation, Typing and Designing)","Sections":{"About":["Language computing matters in this time, and the mother tongue matters most for the common person. This item is to encourage students who are good at Malayalam computing."],"TimeAndFormat":["Part 1: typing a given matter in the fixed time; software judges it. Time: 15 minutes.","Part 2 (HS and HSS/VHSS): lay out the typed matter. Time: 15 minutes."],"Rules":["The competition has two parts. In Part 1 the competitor types a matter given in digital form within the fixed time.","Only competitors who score a fixed percentage enter the second part.","In Part 2 the typed matter is exported, using LibreOffice Writer, to the format given (odt), laid out as instructed and saved.","The illustrations to add are given as resources.","The text for typing has chillus as atomic chillus. Use only the atomic chillu to type chillus."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Both parts get equal weightage. The final result is the total of both scores, taken as out of 100, and gives the place and the grade.","Part 1 (50 score): judged on CPM (characters per minute) and accuracy. Every five wrong key strokes cost one score, taken from the total number of characters typed before CPM is worked out.","Typing score = (CPM of the participant / average CPM of the first three places in the competition) x 50.","Part 2 (50 score): Character formatting 10, Paragraph formatting 20, Inserting apt pictures 10, Page formatting 10. Judged with LibreOffice Writer for layout."],"Points":["Total 100: Part 1 typing 50 and Part 2 layout 50 (HS and HSS/VHSS)."],"Notes":["For UP only the first part of the competition is held. The manual does not print how the UP score is scaled to 100."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Language computing matters in this time, and the mother tongue matters most for the common person. This item is to encourage students who are good at Malayalam computing.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Part 1: typing a given matter in the fixed time; software judges it. Time: 15 minutes.\\n- Part 2 (HS and HSS/VHSS): lay out the typed matter. Time: 15 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The competition has two parts. In Part 1 the competitor types a matter given in digital form within the fixed time.\\n- Only competitors who score a fixed percentage enter the second part.\\n- In Part 2 the typed matter is exported, using LibreOffice Writer, to the format given (odt), laid out as instructed and saved.\\n- The illustrations to add are given as resources.\\n- The text for typing has chillus as atomic chillus. Use only the atomic chillu to type chillus.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Both parts get equal weightage. The final result is the total of both scores, taken as out of 100, and gives the place and the grade.\\n- Part 1 (50 score): judged on CPM (characters per minute) and accuracy. Every five wrong key strokes cost one score, taken from the total number of characters typed before CPM is worked out.\\n- Typing score = (CPM of the participant / average CPM of the first three places in the competition) x 50.\\n- Part 2 (50 score): Character formatting 10, Paragraph formatting 20, Inserting apt pictures 10, Page formatting 10. Judged with LibreOffice Writer for layout.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100: Part 1 typing 50 and Part 2 layout 50 (HS and HSS/VHSS).\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- For UP only the first part of the competition is held. The manual does not print how the UP score is scaled to 100."},{"Title":"Multimedia Presentation","Source":"Manual 2025 ch.10 IT Fair pp.170-171 (c. Multimedia Presentation: Composition and Presentation)","Sections":{"About":["An attractive presentation is as useful as creative writing. Students who prepare their own class or seminar presentation need a multimedia presentation. The item is to encourage students skilled in this field."],"TimeAndFormat":["Part 1: prepare the presentation on the given subject. Time: 1 hour.","Part 2: present it before the panel. Time: 5 minutes."],"Rules":["The competition has two parts.","The themes are published one month before the competition. The subject within the theme is given 10 minutes before the competition starts.","Use LibreOffice Impress on the KITE Ubuntu OS.","Resources for the theme and subject are provided.","The competition is held in a lab with facilities to show the presentation.","The order of presenting is decided by a draw.","A video of the presentation is recorded and used for judging if needed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Part 1, preparing the presentation (80): how well the product conveys the ideas (how effectively ideas on the subject are exchanged) 30; proper use of resources such as pictures and videos 20; proper use of techniques 30.","Part 2, presentation (20): how well ideas are exchanged in the presentation, and how it relates to the presentation made."],"Points":["Total 100: Part 1 presentation 80 and Part 2 delivery 20."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- An attractive presentation is as useful as creative writing. Students who prepare their own class or seminar presentation need a multimedia presentation. The item is to encourage students skilled in this field.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Part 1: prepare the presentation on the given subject. Time: 1 hour.\\n- Part 2: present it before the panel. Time: 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The competition has two parts.\\n- The themes are published one month before the competition. The subject within the theme is given 10 minutes before the competition starts.\\n- Use LibreOffice Impress on the KITE Ubuntu OS.\\n- Resources for the theme and subject are provided.\\n- The competition is held in a lab with facilities to show the presentation.\\n- The order of presenting is decided by a draw.\\n- A video of the presentation is recorded and used for judging if needed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Part 1, preparing the presentation (80): how well the product conveys the ideas (how effectively ideas on the subject are exchanged) 30; proper use of resources such as pictures and videos 20; proper use of techniques 30.\\n- Part 2, presentation (20): how well ideas are exchanged in the presentation, and how it relates to the presentation made.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100: Part 1 presentation 80 and Part 2 delivery 20."},{"Title":"Scratch Programming","Source":"Manual 2025 ch.10 IT Fair pp.175-176 (g. Scratch Project)","Sections":{"About":["Computer programming helps to grow a child's logical thinking. The aim is to make an animation project, games or animation, with Scratch software that a child can use easily."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 1 hour."],"Rules":["Use the Scratch software on the KITE Ubuntu OS (Scratch and Scratch2 must be on the competition computers).","Use pictures that are on the computer or that you make. Pictures from outside are not allowed.","The topic is given 10 minutes before the competition starts.","The competitor makes a visual picture with forms, found or self-made, that suit the topic.","The judges set up the pictures needed for the project on every computer."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Content or theme: 20%.","How attractive it is: 20%.","Modification of sprites, sounds and change of backgrounds: 30%.","Technical excellence (loops, conditions, lists, variables, string processing, number of sprites): 30%."],"Points":["Total 100%: 20, 20, 30 and 30."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Computer programming helps to grow a child's logical thinking. The aim is to make an animation project, games or animation, with Scratch software that a child can use easily.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time: 1 hour.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Use the Scratch software on the KITE Ubuntu OS (Scratch and Scratch2 must be on the competition computers).\\n- Use pictures that are on the computer or that you make. Pictures from outside are not allowed.\\n- The topic is given 10 minutes before the competition starts.\\n- The competitor makes a visual picture with forms, found or self-made, that suit the topic.\\n- The judges set up the pictures needed for the project on every computer.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Content or theme: 20%.\\n- How attractive it is: 20%.\\n- Modification of sprites, sounds and change of backgrounds: 30%.\\n- Technical excellence (loops, conditions, lists, variables, string processing, number of sprites): 30%.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100%: 20, 20, 30 and 30."},{"Title":"Web Page Designing","Source":"Manual 2025 ch.10 IT Fair pp.174-175 (f. Web Site Designing)","Sections":{"About":["The World Wide Web is the most used service on the internet. The competition is to grow the students' ability to make web pages with HTML and CSS."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 1 hour."],"Rules":["Use only HTML and CSS to make the web pages.","The code must be typed in full, using the text editors gedit, xed or pluma, or Geany.","The topic is given 10 minutes before the competition starts.","All the resources needed are on every computer. You may use files you make yourself with KITE OS software, and the pictures, videos and audio files that come with KITE OS.","The product must have more than one page.","Keep the web pages and their related files in the same folder. The paths must be relative, so they work from that folder.","The file name of the home page must be index.html.","A competitor may leave the competition hall only after showing the home page to the judges."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Any software that creates code.","Any other files than the ones listed."],"Judging":["Relation to the content given, correctness and use of language: 20%.","Attractiveness, page layout, ease of reading and elegance: 20%.","Technical excellence (correct tags, navigation, correct links, use of multimedia, number of pages): 40%.","Ease of use: 20%."],"Points":["Total 100%: 20, 20, 40 and 20."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The World Wide Web is the most used service on the internet. The competition is to grow the students' ability to make web pages with HTML and CSS.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time: 1 hour.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Use only HTML and CSS to make the web pages.\\n- The code must be typed in full, using the text editors gedit, xed or pluma, or Geany.\\n- The topic is given 10 minutes before the competition starts.\\n- All the resources needed are on every computer. You may use files you make yourself with KITE OS software, and the pictures, videos and audio files that come with KITE OS.\\n- The product must have more than one page.\\n- Keep the web pages and their related files in the same folder. The paths must be relative, so they work from that folder.\\n- The file name of the home page must be index.html.\\n- A competitor may leave the competition hall only after showing the home page to the judges.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Any software that creates code.\\n- Any other files than the ones listed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Relation to the content given, correctness and use of language: 20%.\\n- Attractiveness, page layout, ease of reading and elegance: 20%.\\n- Technical excellence (correct tags, navigation, correct links, use of multimedia, number of pages): 40%.\\n- Ease of use: 20%.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100%: 20, 20, 40 and 20."},{"Title":"Animation","Source":"Manual 2025 ch.10 IT Fair pp.172-173 (e. Animation)","Sections":{"About":["The aim is to bring out students' creative and artistic skills and introduce them to the animation field. Animation film-making is hard at professional level. The IT books introduce the basic ideas of animation simply, and this item lets interested students find and use these possibilities."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 1 hour."],"Rules":["The topic is given 10 minutes before the competition starts.","Use the Tupi 2D animation software on the KITE Ubuntu OS.","Make an animation of at least 20 seconds.","Export the finished animation to AVI format."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["How the scene relates to the topic, and freshness in showing the idea: 20%.","Form and composition of the characters: 20%.","Use of colours and visual proportions: 20%.","Skill in the technology and effective movement of the characters: 40%."],"Points":["Total 100%: 20, 20, 20 and 40."],"Notes":["Judge the work as students' work, not as professional work."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The aim is to bring out students' creative and artistic skills and introduce them to the animation field. Animation film-making is hard at professional level. The IT books introduce the basic ideas of animation simply, and this item lets interested students find and use these possibilities.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time: 1 hour.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The topic is given 10 minutes before the competition starts.\\n- Use the Tupi 2D animation software on the KITE Ubuntu OS.\\n- Make an animation of at least 20 seconds.\\n- Export the finished animation to AVI format.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- How the scene relates to the topic, and freshness in showing the idea: 20%.\\n- Form and composition of the characters: 20%.\\n- Use of colours and visual proportions: 20%.\\n- Skill in the technology and effective movement of the characters: 40%.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100%: 20, 20, 20 and 40.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Judge the work as students' work, not as professional work."}]`),s=[{Title:"Malayalam Typing",AgeGroup:"IT UP",Source:"Manual 2025 ch.10 IT Fair p.168",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["UP students do only the first part (typing). The second part (layout) is only for HS and HSS/VHSS."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- UP students do only the first part (typing). The second part (layout) is only for HS and HSS/VHSS.`}],r=[{Key:"Website",Kind:"link",Label:"Sasthrolsavam entry and item list site",Value:"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/",Source:"Item list 2026 (KITE)"},{Key:"EventDates",Kind:"text",Label:"Dates of the fair",Value:"To be announced. Each level is held on the dates in the education calendar the General Education Department publishes every year, or as the Director of General Education directs. The manual prints no dates.",Source:"Manual 2025 p.1 (chapter 1)"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Venue",Value:{Name:"To be announced",Address:"",City:"Kerala",MapUrl:"",Directions:"The state venue is decided by the Director of General Education. A school is chosen by the committee for each lower level."},Source:"Manual 2025 pp.9, 12, 16 (venue of each level)"},{Key:"SubDistrictRegistrationFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Registration fee at sub-district level",Value:"Rs 20 per student, collected only from students of classes 9, 10, 11 and 12",Source:"Manual 2025 p.11 (Sub-district, money collection)"},{Key:"AppealFeeSchool",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee at school level",Value:"No appeal fee at school level",Source:"Manual 2025 p.30"},{Key:"AppealFeeSubDistrict",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee at sub-district level",Value:"Rs 1,000",Source:"Manual 2025 pp.30, 32"},{Key:"AppealFeeRevenueDistrict",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee at revenue district level",Value:"Rs 1,500",Source:"Manual 2025 pp.30, 32"},{Key:"AppealFeeState",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee at state level",Value:"Rs 2,000",Source:"Manual 2025 pp.30, 33"},{Key:"AppealFeeHigher",Kind:"fee",Label:"Higher appeal fee",Value:"Rs 2,500",Source:"Manual 2025 p.30"},{Key:"CertificateReissueFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Fee for a new certificate if the issued one is lost or has errors",Value:"Rs 250 demand draft in the name of the Director of General Education",Source:"Manual 2025 p.6 rule 16"},{Key:"AppealTimeLimit",Kind:"text",Label:"Time limit for an appeal",Value:"Within one hour after the results are announced",Source:"Manual 2025 p.30 (chapter 4 rule 3)"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed in the manual",Value:[{Date:"2025-09-12",Title:"Revised Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 is in force",Text:"The Additional Director (Academic) of the General Education Department ordered on 12 September 2025 that the revised manual be used, and that the fairs from school level to state level follow it. The manual replaces all earlier science, maths, social science, work experience and IT fair manuals and rules.",Url:""},{Date:"",Title:"IT Fair has no Lower Primary level",Text:"The IT Fair is held for UP, HS and HSS/VHSS students only.",Url:""}],Source:"DGE order of 12-09-2025; manual p.1 and ch.10"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, levels, eligibility, entry, appeals, championship, judging and the IT Fair items with their times, software and marking criteria are read in full from the Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 of the General Education Department, Kerala.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 (chapters 1-5, 10, Annexure I)",Url:"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/entry_forms/sasthrolsavam_manual_2025.pdf"},{Claim:"Item names, item codes (UP: Digital Painting 386, Malayalam Typing 387, IT Quiz 388; HS: 389-394 and Animation 425; HSS/VHSS: 395-399 and 426-427), single-participant items open to all genders.",SourceType:"Primary - the organiser's official item list",Source:"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Item List 2026, KITE",Url:"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/index.php/Home/item_list"}],c={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:t,Page:a,ParticipantTypes:i,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:n,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{o as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,n as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,a as Page,i as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,h as Year,c as default};
